cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use AgentPause in your research, please cite it as below. Results produced
  with the simulator are simulated; AgentPause has not yet been evaluated with human participants.
type: software
title: "AgentPause: Research Infrastructure for Adaptive Human Intervention Timing in AI Agents"
abstract: >-
  An open-source toolkit for studying when an AI agent should continue autonomously and
  when it should pause and involve a human. It provides a decision engine with baseline and
  adaptive intervention policies, explanations of why and when an intervention happens,
  a deterministic simulator with ground-truth labels, experiment and study tooling,
  a REST API, SDKs, and a web interface.
authors:
  - family-names: Kaviani
    given-names: Morvarid
  - name: AgentPause contributors
version: 0.1.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/morvaridkaviani/AgentPause"
url: "https://github.com/morvaridkaviani/AgentPause"
date-released: "2026-10-15"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - human-AI interaction
  - mixed-initiative interaction
  - AI agents
  - interruption management
  - human oversight
  - explainable AI
